# How much of beef's carbon footprint is transport?
subtitle: "Guess how much of beef's climate footprint comes from transport, then see why what you eat matters far more than where it comes from."
tags: ["food","earth","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Local beef saves the planet?\" stamp \"MYTH?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Leda | a youthful, bright quiz host; curious, not overexcited","b":"gemini:Enceladus | a co-host who is genuinely amazed; natural, never exaggerated","take":"lines"}

## How much of beef's carbon footprint is transport?
affirm: playful
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Transport
      - Other
      - Waste
      - Land use
      - Farm
    values:
      - 0.5
      - 5.1
      - 14.4
      - 23.2
      - 56.2
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 110
    y_label: kg CO₂e per kg of beef
    bar_colors: same
    label_size: 30
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: You want to reduce the carbon footprint of your food? Focus on what you eat, not whether your food is local
      authors: Hannah Ritchie (Our World in Data)
      year: 2020
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/food-choice-vs-eating-local
      finding: transport is under 10% of most foods' emissions and 0.5% for beef from beef herds; in EU diets food transport is 6% of emissions; swapping less than one day a week of beef and dairy calories beats buying all food locally (Weber & Matthews 2008); air freight is 0.16% of food miles but emits about 50 times more than a boat per tonne-km
    - id: chain
      title: 'Food: greenhouse gas emissions across the supply chain (chart)'
      authors: Our World in Data, from Poore & Nemecek (2018), Science
      year: 2018
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/food-emissions-supply-chain
      finding: 'beef (beef herd), kg CO2e per kg: farm 56.2, land use 23.2, losses 14.4, animal feed 2.7, processing 1.8, packaging 0.35, retail 0.23, transport 0.49'

    icon burger size 280 set twemoji x 300 y 430 icon_look picture of hamburger hidden true
    icon truck size 280 set twemoji x 700 y 430 icon_look picture of "delivery truck" hidden true
    path total dashed thick #8f887c points [[-0.5,99.4],[4.5,99.4]] data true hidden true
    label total_l "total ≈ 100 kg" below-right #8f887c attach_to total cites ["chain"] font_size 40 hidden true
    text pct "0.5%" above bar_1 gap 20 #b5482e cites ["owid"] font_size 52 hidden true
    icon plane size 140 set twemoji x 230 y 245 icon_look picture of airplane hidden true
    icon ship size 140 set twemoji x 460 y 245 icon_look picture of ship hidden true
    shape r_air #b5482e shape rect x 230 y 470 width 130 height 300 style.fill #f3d9d3 hidden true
    shape r_sea #2f6b8f shape rect x 460 y 324 width 130 height 7 style.fill #cfe3ee hidden true
    text l_air "50×" right r_air gap 20 #b5482e cites ["owid"] font_size 64 hidden true
    text l_sea "1×" above r_sea gap 20 #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] font_size 56 hidden true

    card title "Beef's footprint: how much is transport?"

A: Quick one: how much of a beef burger's climate footprint comes from getting it to you?
    draw burger truck

B: Loads, surely. Lorries, ships, planes. That's why I buy local.
    highlight truck

    erase burger truck

A: Let's see. A kilo of beef puts out about a hundred kilos of greenhouse gases, all told.
    draw axes total total_l

    ask "Drag the transport bar to your guess." on bar_1 store g default "30" tolerance 0.02
        right: Good guess: about half a kilo of the hundred.
        wrong: It's about half a kilo: a sliver.

B: Half a kilo? Then where's the other ninety-nine?
    highlight bar_1

A: Mostly the farm: cows burp methane, plus manure and feed. Then forest cleared for pasture.
    draw bar_5 bar_4

B: Let me guess the rest: meat that gets thrown away, and the packaging.
    draw bar_3 bar_2

A: Spot on. So transport is half a percent. Local beef is still almost all cow.
    draw pct

    erase axes bar_1 bar_2 bar_3 bar_4 bar_5 total total_l pct

B: So food miles never matter?
    draw plane r_air l_air ship r_sea l_sea

A: By air they do: fifty times a ship's emissions for the same load. Berries, asparagus. But almost all food goes by sea.
    highlight r_air

A: And one US study found that swapping beef and dairy for chicken or beans just one day a week cuts more than buying everything local.
    icon cal size 230 set twemoji x 790 y 520 icon_look picture of "spiral calendar"
    text l_cal "1 meatless day" below cal gap 20 #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] font_size 48
    text l_gt "> all local" below l_cal gap 10 #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] font_size 56

B: Fine. Farmers' market on Saturday, no burger on Monday.
    highlight cal

